      <description>&lt;p&gt;After achieving RCE on the &lt;code&gt;SQL&lt;/code&gt; host I proceeded to check the user&amp;rsquo;s privileges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;https://emc2hf.github.io/images/goad/3-amsi-bypass/mssql_whoami_priv.png&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;

As this is a service account it has the &lt;code&gt;SeImpersonatePrivilege&lt;/code&gt; privilege enabled. This is a direct pwn using the Potato or the PrintSpoofer binaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowing the way I will get &lt;code&gt;NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM&lt;/code&gt; on the &lt;strong&gt;SQL&lt;/strong&gt; host, I proceeded to check if &lt;strong&gt;Defender&lt;/strong&gt; is active.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;https://emc2hf.github.io/images/goad/3-amsi-bypass/mssql_check_defender.png&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I also confirmed I can access Kali from the Windows environment with an HTTP request:
